->Stack is also used in tree traversal. It is used to implement the iterative Preorder, postorder and inorder.
In iterative preoder (Data Left Right)
->we initialise a stack which stores the pointer the Tree Node.
->push the root into the stack.
->create a pointer pointing to the top of the stack and pop the top() and print.
->we check for the right child, if present we push it and then we push the left child if available.
->Repeat the process again.
<---------------------------------------------->
void iterativePreorder(TreeNode* root) {
    if ( root == NULL) return;

    stack<TreeNode*> st;

    st.push(root);


    while (!st.empty()) {
        TreeNode* current = st.top();
        st.pop();

        cout << current->data << endl;

        if (current->right)
            st.push(current->right);

        if (current->left)
            st.push(current->left);
    }
}
